  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.PostgresqlProperties\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A Spring Boot configuration properties class that holds settings pertaining to the PostgreSQL database connection. Annotated with @ConfigurationProperties(prefix = 'postgresql'), it binds external configuration properties (e.g., from application.properties or application.yml) with the prefix 'postgresql' to its fields. It encapsulates four connection-related properties: (1) username – the database username, accessed via getUsername()/setUsername(); (2) password – the database password, accessed via getPassword()/setPassword(); (3) driverClass – the JDBC driver class name, accessed via getDriverClass()/setDriverClass(); and (4) url – the JDBC connection URL, accessed via getUrl()/setUrl(). All fields follow standard JavaBean conventions with getter/setter pairs, enabling Spring's property binding mechanism to populate them automatically at application startup.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/PostgresqlProperties.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
